WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.795
Production containers should be observable without carrying unnecessary debug tools or exposing sensitive data.

2
00:00:07.795 --> 00:00:20.680
Runtime images should not include shells, package managers, debug utilities, source code, test data, or secret-bearing artifacts unless there is a justified and reviewed operational need.

3
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:26.724
Logs should flow to the platform logging pipeline and be safe for centralized collection.

4
00:00:26.724 --> 00:00:39.450
They should avoid tokens, connection strings, cookies, authorization headers, raw request bodies, secret environment variables, mounted secret contents, and sensitive business data.

5
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:48.597
Structured logs should include safe context such as operation name, correlation ID, image version, environment, and dependency name.

6
00:00:48.597 --> 00:00:57.108
Debug endpoints, diagnostic ports, crash dumps, tracing, and metrics should be environment-scoped and access-controlled.

7
00:00:57.108 --> 00:01:09.277
A diagnostic feature that is appropriate in development may be inappropriate in production without access controls, redaction, retention rules, and incident handling guidance.

8
00:01:09.277 --> 00:01:24.627
Useful operational signals include container health, restart count, memory usage, CPU pressure, socket usage, failed probes, startup time, image version, deployment metadata, dependency errors, and configuration source.

9
00:01:24.627 --> 00:01:33.456
These signals help teams distinguish application faults, platform constraints, dependency problems, and deployment mistakes.

10
00:01:33.456 --> 00:01:48.329
Production review should cover image choice, Dockerfile design, user identity, writable paths, secrets, ports, probes, resource limits, image scanning, registry controls, logging, rollback, and incident response.

11
00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:56.442
A secure container release is not only a Dockerfile; it is a lifecycle that keeps build, runtime, and operations aligned.
